Z||000000||AusFiero||09-13-2001||08:02 PM||||Well that was quick service by an insurance company if I ever seen it. My Fiero has been declared a total loss and I have bought it back for AU$2000. The insurance company is paying out the full $25,000 insured value so as you can imagine I am going to rebuild. I had over $32,000 in that car but thems the breaks. Getting it back will at least give me lots of parts. That car is not getting rebuilt, but another one I have my sights set on. The other is an 86 SE with t-tops also which will make me the owner of half of Australias t-topped cars. Well thats if the owner ever decides to return one of my calls. Stage 2 has been set back but I have salvaged enough to get it back on track within the month. <P>Now where can I find a supercharged 3.8 Buick fast. Anyone make kits to fit them? <P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||14
